.TH REMPKG 1 "September 2026" "REM developer tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rempkg \- create, install, inspect and verify local REM packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rempkg
.B pack
.I directory archive.rmpkg
.br
.B rempkg
.B install
[\fB--root \fIdir\fR]
.I archive.rmpkg
.br
.B rempkg
.B remove
[\fB--root \fIdir\fR]
.I name
.br
.B rempkg
.B list|verify
[\fB--root \fIdir\fR]
[\fIname\fR]
.br
.B rempkg
.B info
[\fB--root \fIdir\fR]
.I name-or-archive
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rempkg
is a local Python 3 package prototype. Packages use a gzip-compressed tar
archive with JSON metadata, a SHA-256 manifest and a payload tree. Installed
ownership records are kept under /var/lib/rempkg.
.SH SAFETY
Installation refuses to overwrite existing files. Removal refuses to delete
files that are missing or changed from the recorded manifest. The tool does
not authenticate packages, resolve dependencies, run hooks, or recover a
multi-file install after power loss. Install only trusted archives and retain
a separate rootfs backup.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rempkg pack hello-package hello-1.0.rmpkg
rempkg info hello-1.0.rmpkg
rempkg install hello-1.0.rmpkg
rempkg verify
rempkg remove hello
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
REM_PACKAGE_SYSTEM.md
